WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.500
(futuristic sound)

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.133
- Awesome, we have our
scene setup here and you

3
00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:10.533
can see the cool sky box all around it to

4
00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:13.466
create this cool nighttime
effect at the bottom.

5
00:00:13.466 --> 00:00:16.300
So we're gonna do a little
bit more scene setup.

6
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.033
So, in this game, what
we're actually gonna do is

7
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:23.066
we're gonna use one of
our primitive shapes.

8
00:00:23.066 --> 00:00:26.066
So in our hierarchy, we
can go to the top

9
00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:28.700
or right click in the hierarchy,

10
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.366
so we're gonna make a 3D
object and we're going to

11
00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.900
make a sphere.

12
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.866
Now, you can see our sphere is floating off

13
00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:41.400
onto the side so that's
definitely not good.

14
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.066
So what we're gonna do first is we're just

15
00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:48.000
going to reset this back
to the center of our world.

16
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.433
So I'm just going to
use the icon on the

17
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:52.633
right side of transform.

18
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:55.933
Click on it and then reset position.

19
00:00:55.933 --> 00:00:59.000
And there you go, now our
sphere is exactly in the center.

20
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:00.633
I'm just going to rename this because this

21
00:01:00.633 --> 00:01:02.900
will actually be what our player controls

22
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.233
so this will be the player.

23
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:10.600
Now, if you can see our little sphere,

24
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:13.966
if we focus on it with
F, it's kind of small.

25
00:01:13.966 --> 00:01:16.433
Especially in the game view.

26
00:01:16.433 --> 00:01:19.133
So what we're going to do is
we're just gonna scale it up.

27
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.833
So we'll actually just
set all of these values

28
00:01:21.833 --> 00:01:24.600
on the X,Y, and Z to 1.5 manually.

29
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.066
That looks pretty good.

30
00:01:31.066 --> 00:01:33.466
Let's see, we have a
little bit of clipping

31
00:01:33.466 --> 00:01:34.900
through the ground so
we're actually just going

32
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:37.400
to move the sphere up a little bit

33
00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:39.533
so that way it's at
least above the ground.

34
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.333
So now that we have our
sphere in the world here,

35
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:44.633
we're going to use a rigid body

36
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:46.666
so we can actually use
physics and then gravity

37
00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:50.200
will actually make this
sphere fall onto this plane.

38
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.766
So we're going to go to the
inspector on the right side

39
00:01:53.766 --> 00:01:57.300
click add component, type in rigid,

40
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.633
so we have our rigid
body and we apply that

41
00:02:00.633 --> 00:02:03.633
and it already uses
gravity which is great.

42
00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:07.166
And then one little bit of
setup that we're gonna do is

43
00:02:07.166 --> 00:02:12.166
we're actually going to apply
textures onto this object now.

44
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.900
So, if we go to our project
window and then we go

45
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:20.233
to our textures folder
underneath our course library,

46
00:02:20.233 --> 00:02:23.400
if we expand that you can
see all of these different

47
00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.100
textures that we have,
so similarly to how we

48
00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:29.733
could apply textures to
some of our background

49
00:02:29.733 --> 00:02:33.000
scenes we can actually apply
textures onto our characters.

50
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.233
So, I'm going to, in this
case, let's see let's try

51
00:02:37.233 --> 00:02:39.566
this checkered texture.

52
00:02:39.566 --> 00:02:41.933
So I can just drag it
directly onto the player

53
00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:44.500
and it will immediately
change the texture.

54
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.700
Or, I can take on of the
other textures and I can

55
00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.700
drag it directly onto
our object in the scene

56
00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.700
and it'll change it that way.

57
00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.833
So texture mapping is
a really useful way to

58
00:02:55.833 --> 00:02:58.166
be able to apply different textures

59
00:02:58.166 --> 00:03:00.066
and materials onto our objects.

60
00:03:00.066 --> 00:03:04.766
If we wanted to make our ball shinier

61
00:03:04.766 --> 00:03:07.600
or use a different color
or something like that

62
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:09.866
we can use texture maps
to be able to do so.

63
00:03:10.966 --> 00:03:12.333
So, what you're gonna do is you're gonna

64
00:03:12.333 --> 00:03:15.033
go into your hierarchy, right click,

65
00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:19.766
create a 3D object, and
we're going to make a sphere.

66
00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:24.766
And then your sphere you're
going to rename to player.

67
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.366
You're going to reset the position so that

68
00:03:28.366 --> 00:03:30.866
it's back at 000.

69
00:03:30.866 --> 00:03:35.866
Scale up your sphere to
be 1.5 on the X,Y, and Z.

70
00:03:37.966 --> 00:03:40.133
And then you're probably
going to want to reposition

71
00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.866
your sphere on the Y axis.

72
00:03:43.866 --> 00:03:46.366
Then you're going to add a rigid body.

73
00:03:46.366 --> 00:03:47.666
And then last but not least you're gonna

74
00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:50.700
go into your assets in the course library

75
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.766
in your textures folder
and you're going to

76
00:03:52.766 --> 00:03:55.266
click and drag a texture
either onto the player

77
00:03:55.266 --> 00:03:57.733
in the hierarchy or in the scene view.

78
00:03:57.733 --> 00:03:59.766
Now it's your turn.

79
00:03:59.766 --> 00:04:02.700
(futuristic sound)
